abstract: >-
  Exact-arithmetic computational supplement for the finite census results in
  Part V of the book "The Landscape Is the Meaning" and in the preprint
  "Variable Elimination for Prime-Implicate 0-1 Relaxations of Boolean
  Constraints". Every count is produced by exact rational arithmetic with no
  floating point. The three-port census (240 signed-ideal of 256 regimes, 22
  signed-shuffle orbits, the sixteen non-ideal regimes in two orbits of eight,
  fractional vertex (1/2,1/2,1/2)) is reproducible from the Python standard
  library alone, with no third-party dependency and no network; an independent
  third-party reimplementation and its recorded output are included. The
  four- and five-port material, the recorded certificates and the n=5 orbit
  census are also here, the certificate verifier requiring pycddlib.
identifiers:
